{:event/id "39bf764b-0441-4cfd-bdd8-f1511d2d1d95" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/at "2026-09-25T13:43:04Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/resource-refresh-generalizes-debounce-to-latest-pending-intent :finding/shapes #{:debounce :cell :lifecycle :infra} :finding/current-name "resource-watch-timer* + schedule-resource-refresh! / event-runtime reload-timer* + debounced-reload!" :finding/candidate-name "LatestPendingIntent<Action>" :finding/claim "The resource watcher independently repeats the event-runtime debounce law: each new refresh intent cancels the prior timer, installs one replacement timer, and clears the timer cell before the effect begins. Because the fresh occurrence protects an index refresh rather than a lifecycle transition, the parent name DebouncedTransitionIntent<Action> is too narrow. The shared law is only latest-pending intent coalescing; it neither shares an in-flight effect nor memoizes completion."}}
{:event/id "75ebb10a-cca9-4522-83ba-0921144bf93a" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["39bf764b-0441-4cfd-bdd8-f1511d2d1d95"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/at "2026-09-25T13:43:04Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/resource-watcher-is-handle-backed-restartable-set :finding/shapes #{:lifecycle :registry :handle :infra} :finding/current-name "resource-watchers* + resource-watch-running?* + start-resource-watcher!/stop-resource-watcher!" :finding/candidate-name "HandleBackedRestartableSet<Handle>" :finding/claim "The resource watcher is an independently restartable subsystem whose running state is backed by retained OS watcher handles. Start is idempotent while marked running; stop cancels a pending refresh, closes every retained handle, clears the handle set, and resets running so a later start is lawful. This pressure-tests restartability but not the parent's fail-closed policy gate: resource-watcher activation has no independent policy-refusal predicate, so RestartableRuntimeGate<Subsystem> should not be generalized from restartability alone."}}
{:event/id "cad40d07-8f04-45d6-a7e9-9c5ed98b72a8" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["75ebb10a-cca9-4522-83ba-0921144bf93a"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:eaa3e951-db0c-4432-96d5-e3e61ce39816" :event/at "2026-09-25T13:43:04Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/resource-watcher-activation-keeps-successful-subset :finding/shapes #{:lifecycle :projection :reconciler :infra} :finding/current-name "start-resource-watcher! root watch loop" :finding/candidate-name "BestEffortSubsetActivation<Desired,Active>" :finding/claim "Watcher startup derives desired existing resource roots, attempts each OS watch independently, converts a failed root into nil, retains every successful handle, and marks the subsystem running whenever at least one handle exists. Successful siblings are not rolled back when another root fails, and this subsystem exposes no per-root activation-status projection. It therefore independently confirms non-transactional partial activation while countering promotion of PartialActivationStatus<Component> as a universal status shape."}}
